          "explanation": "The reported weakness is a specific confusion between base rate (prevalence) and sensitivity (true positive rate). This is best addressed by one integrated lesson that names and distinguishes the two quantities while deriving and applying Bayes' rule, followed by a changed medical-test example the learner solves independently. No readiness history exists, so a small diagnostic element is built into the first activity rather than a separate relearning phase. Remediation is contingent on observed failure in the changed example, not pre-booked.",
          "recommendedEffort": {
            "lowMinutes": 55,
            "likelyMinutes": 75,
            "highMinutes": 100
          },
          "phases": [
            {
              "localId": "phase_learn",
              "title": "Distinguish base rate from sensitivity and derive Bayes' rule",
              "outcome": "Can state the difference between base rate and sensitivity and write Bayes' rule for a diagnostic test.",
              "readinessCriterion": "Learner correctly labels prevalence and sensitivity in a worked example and writes the posterior formula without prompting."
            },
            {
              "localId": "phase_apply",
              "title": "Apply Bayes' rule to a changed medical-test example",
              "outcome": "Correctly computes the posterior probability in a changed example and explains the role of the base rate.",
              "readinessCriterion": "Learner produces the correct posterior and a correct explanation that does not swap base rate and sensitivity."
            }
          ]
        },
        "scope": [
          {
            "scopeRef": "scope_1",
            "disposition": "INCLUDED",
            "contribution": "Names and contrasts base rate (prevalence) and conditional probability (sensitivity) as the core source of the reported confusion."
          },
          {
            "scopeRef": "scope_2",
            "disposition": "INCLUDED",
            "contribution": "Derives and states Bayes' rule so the posterior is computed from the base rate and test characteristics rather than conflated with them."
